      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done.\n\n\u003e Should it be ACTIVE_RW?\n\nActive is used differently from \u0027running\u0027. Active/non-active is tied to flash slots. Running image can be RO, RW_A, RW_B but active image can only be RW_A or RW_B. So, I think it\u0027s redundant to add _RW for the same reason it is so to name EC_FLASH_REGION_UPDATE_RW. RO always runs. So, I see it permanently \u0027active\u0027 (even when RW is running). In recovery mode, an active RW image doesn\u0027t enter \u0027running\u0027 state but it\u0027s still active on the flash.  I can copy this comment to the code if you prefer. I use \u0027active\u0027 to mean \u0027scheduled-to-run\u0027.",
      "parentUuid": "27c09d49_5e5ea14b",
